  <name>Alpine MTB Map</name>
  <description><![CDATA[Lift-served mountain-bike spots across the Alps and the Jura, down to the Mercantour above Nice, plus a handful of the world's best-known parks further afield. Each main pin gives what it costs to get up, what the trails are like, and how long it takes to get there - from whichever city a rider would actually start from. Blue pins are purpose-built bike parks, dark green pins are natural lift-served spots, and brown pins are the ones you pedal up. A few spots stay ridable in winter. Lines are trail geometries from OpenStreetMap (ODbL) - treat them as indicative, not as a substitute for on-site signage. Compiled July 2026.]]></description>
  <visibility>1</visibility>
  <Placemark>
    <name>St-Cergue / La Dôle (Jura vaudois) [train fare only]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>La Givrine (top of the NStCM train)</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>The closest real singletrack riding to Lausanne. Three marked descents drop off the Jura crest back towards Arzier and St-Cergue: Mont Chaubert, Mont Bailly (plus an eastern variant) and La Plagne. Rooty, rocky, north-facing forest trails, short (1-2 km each) but you can chain them and pedal back up in 20-30 min, or reload with the train. Dry quickly, ridable from April to November - the best shoulder-season option on this map.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift needed: the train is the climb (Nyon 400 m > La Givrine 1228 m). Normal CFF/NStCM fare, plus a bike ticket - the national day bike pass is about 14 CHF (bikes are carried on the NStCM, space is limited at peak times).<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h05</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.nstcm.ch/">NStCM railway</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>6.111707,46.454526,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
