  <Placemark>
    <name>Les Pléiades (above Vevey) [train fare only]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Les Pléiades station (top of the MVR rack railway)</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>No bike park, no shuttle circus - just a 750 m vertical drop of forest tracks and singletrack back down to Blonay, Les Chevalleyres or Lally. Mellow, green, family-friendly gradients with a couple of steeper trail options in the woods above Blonay. Good first outing of the season, and you can extend north towards Les Paccots.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No dedicated bike pass: it is a normal public-transport ticket (Vevey > Les Pleiades is a short-distance fare, roughly 12-14 CHF one way full price) plus a bike ticket, ~14 CHF for the day pass. Cheap day out.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.mob.ch/">MOB transport</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>6.909920,46.483244,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>pleiades</value></Data>
      <Data name="tags"><value>beginner natural</value></Data>
      <Data name="open_from"><value>04-01</value></Data>
      <Data name="closed_from"><value>12-01</value></Data>
      <mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon>
      <mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Chaumont (Neuchâtel) [city fare, ~5 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Chaumont - top of the La Coudre funicular</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Chaumont bike park: a proper DH line with 110+ doubles and around 20 drops, clearly aimed at experienced riders - but a chicken line runs alongside the whole way so you can pick your level. Back down to La Coudre it alternates forest doubletrack and singletrack. Open all year, which makes it the winter fallback when the Alps are shut.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The funicular is part of the Neuchatel city network (transN / Onde Verte): a few francs per ride, so this is by far the cheapest lift-served riding in the region. Runs year-round, every 15-30 min.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure (normally open year-round).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train + funicular</td><td>~1h10</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.transn.ch/">TransN</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>6.957526,47.026524,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>chaumont</value></Data>
