  <Placemark>
    <name>Moléson-sur-Gruyères [38 CHF / Magic Pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Plan-Francey 1520 m - bike park base</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Bike Park Moleson, based at Plan-Francey and served by the funicular then the chairlift. Modzon and Poya are the flowy, accessible runs - genuinely good for progressing riders. Tche Don is the technical enduro line, steeper and rougher. Small park, but well built, rarely crowded, and the Gruyeres backdrop is hard to beat.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Journee bike (funicular + cable car + chairlift) 38 CHF; a 4-hour bike ticket (funicular + chairlift) is 29 CHF. Free with the Magic Pass.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 May; closed from 2 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~1h40</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.moleson.ch/en/">Moleson</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
