  <Placemark>
    <name>Villars-Gryon - Col de Bretaye [36 CHF / Magic Pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Col de Bretaye 1806 m - top of the Villars cog railway</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>The Grand Chamossaire descent, opened in summer 2025: 3 km of blue flow with big berms, a few technical sections and smooth fast bits between them - built for families and improving riders rather than for hucking. Around it sits a dense network of marked SuisseMobile routes: 573 Bretaye > Villars, 572 Bretaye > Ollon (a long 20 km+ descent to the Rhone valley), 580 towards Les Chaux and Solalex, and 582 Taveyanne-Solalex.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>TVGD summer day pass 36 CHF adult / 18 CHF child, covering the Villars-Bretaye train, the gondolas and the Grand Chamossaire chairlift. Single ascent 20 CHF. Free with the Magic Pass. Mid-June to late October.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 26 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.villars-diablerets.ch/en/Z12514/mountain-bike">Villars-Diablerets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>7.073167,46.321886,0</coordinates></Point>
