  <Placemark>
    <name>Les Diablerets [36 CHF / Magic Pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Meilleret 1949 m - top of the chairlift</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Isenau Bike (SuisseMobile route 590) is the classic: an 8 km climb out of the village, then a descent split between a vehicle-width track and a forest path that asks for some skill. If you do not fancy the technical part, the tarmac road back to Les Diablerets is right there. Stage 2 of the Alpes du Leman Bike route continues from here down to Bex.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Same TVGD day pass as Villars, 36 CHF, free with the Magic Pass. Important caveat: the old Isenau gondola was dismantled and has not been replaced, so the Meilleret chairlift is the summer lift here - check it is actually turning before you commit.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 July; closed from 1 September (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h25</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.villars-diablerets.ch/en/Z12514/mountain-bike">Villars-Diablerets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>7.121228,46.333290,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>diablerets</value></Data>
      <Data name="tags"><value>beginner magicpass natural</value></Data>
      <Data name="open_from"><value>07-01</value></Data>
      <Data name="closed_from"><value>09-01</value></Data>
      <Data name="price_day"><value>36 CHF</value></Data>
      <mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon>
      <mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Diablerets: Isenau Bike (590)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[15.4 km. Geometry from OpenStreetMap relation 27184 (ODbL) - indicative only, follow the signs on the ground.]]></description>
