  <Placemark>
    <name>Bienne / Magglingen - BielTrail [16 CHF with Half Fare]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Magglingen/Macolin - top of the funicular</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>BielTrail is a 1.95 km, 440 m descent running point-to-point back towards the funicular. Most of the main line is fast, flowing and well maintained, but it includes a short black section that is genuinely technical: a steep downhill passage through rocks and roots. Additional, more relaxed paths descend through the same area, but these are shared with hikers rather than bike-only trails: slow down, give way and expect people around blind corners. The wider Jura network (Les Pres-d'Orvin Bike 844, Erguel Bike 843) starts from the same plateau if you want more distance.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Magglingen funicular is part of Biel city transport. A day costs 16 CHF with the Swiss Half Fare Travelcard, making repeated laps unusually good value. There is a bike wash behind the lower funicular station.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure in a typical year; avoid riding when the ground is saturated and check local conditions.<br/>Daily opening hours: 05:45-00:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train + funicular</td><td>~1h25</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.biel-bienne.ch/en/bieltrail.html/2943">City of Biel</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
