  <Placemark>
    <name>Portes du Soleil - Champéry / Les Crosets [from 26 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Planachaux 1800 m - top of the Champéry cable car</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>The gateway to 600 km of marked MTB trails and 21 open lifts - the biggest lift-linked bike area within reach of Lausanne. Champery has hosted UCI World Cup downhill, and the Grand Conche black DH off Les Crosets is the serious local line. From Planachaux you can ride the whole loop into France (Chatel, Morzine, Les Gets, Avoriaz) on one pass - the Pass'Portes weekend, 26-28 June 2026, is the day to do it.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Swiss-side day passes start around 26 CHF for a single sector; the Champery cable car alone is from 18 CHF. A full Portes du Soleil day bike pass (both countries, 21 lifts) is 39 EUR, and a PdS season bike pass starts at 335 CHF.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 12 June; closed from 14 September (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h50</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://en.portesdusoleil.com/summer/mountain-biking/">Portes du Soleil</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>6.845206,46.175042,0</coordinates></Point>
