  <Placemark>
    <name>Chur - Brambrueesch [from 53 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Brambrueesch 1600 m - top of the Chur cable car</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>The valley-floor member of the Bike Kingdom, and the one to pick if the weather up high looks bad. Four built flow trails drop off Brambrueesch back into town: Brambi Flow and Chur Flow are the easy, jumpy ones, Alpen Ride is longer and more natural, and Rock'n'Roll is the rough one. Around 1000 m of descent, straight into a city with trains home.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Covered by the same Bike Kingdom ticket, from 53 CHF. The cable car starts inside the city, so there is no bus and no transfer at the far end.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 May; closed from 2 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~3h45</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.chur.graubuenden.ch/en/activities/summer/mountain-biking">Chur tourism</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>9.516227,46.828967,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>chur</value></Data>
      <Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bikepark</value></Data>
      <Data name="open_from"><value>05-15</value></Data>
      <Data name="closed_from"><value>11-02</value></Data>
      <Data name="price_day"><value>53 CHF</value></Data>
      <mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon>
      <mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Chur: Brambrueeschbahn valley station</name>
    <description><![CDATA[In the middle of Chur, ten minutes' walk from the main railway station. Probably the easiest lift-served riding to reach by train in Switzerland.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-gray</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>9.525755,46.847324,0</coordinates></Point>
