  <Placemark>
    <name>Interlaken - Harder Kulm [funicular, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Harder Kulm 1322 m - top of the funicular</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>The Harder Downhill: a steep, relentless 700 m drop off Interlaken's local peak straight back into town. Tight, rooty switchbacks through the forest with a couple of genuinely exposed sections - not a first bike park, but the view over the Thunersee and Brienzersee on the way up is worth the ticket on its own.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Harderbahn funicular leaves a few minutes' walk from Interlaken Ost. Bike carriage is limited and the 2026 fare is not confirmed here - check jungfrau.ch, and note the funicular is primarily a tourist ride, so expect queues at midday.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-21:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~2h20</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.jungfrau.ch/en-gb/harder-kulm/">Jungfrau Railways</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
