  <Placemark>
    <name>Grindelwald - First [Firstbahn, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>First 2168 m - top of the Firstbahn</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>15 km and 1100 m of descent from First back to Grindelwald on natural paths and tracks, under the north face of the Eiger the whole way. Not a built bike park - this is a big mountain descent with a gondola instead of a climb, and it splits naturally at Bort if you want a shorter day.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Firstbahn gondola. Bike carriage and the exact 2026 fare are not confirmed here - check jungfrau.ch. Adventure packages bundling unlimited gondola use with activities are usually the better value if you are staying.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 26 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-17:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~3h00</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.jungfrau.ch/en-gb/grindelwaldfirst/">Grindelwald-First</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>8.052960,46.661377,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>grindelwald</value></Data>
      <Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert natural</value></Data>
      <Data name="open_from"><value>06-15</value></Data>
      <Data name="closed_from"><value>10-26</value></Data>
