  <Placemark>
    <name>Aletsch Arena - Riederalp / Bettmeralp / Fiescheralp [cable cars, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bettmeralp - car-free village above the Rhone</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>A high sunny terrace above the Rhone valley, looking straight at the Aletsch glacier. The Flowtrail Wurzenbord is the built one; otherwise this is big-view touring, linking Riederalp, Bettmeralp and Martisberg, or pushing on from Fiescheralp to the Marjela. Not steep-and-gnarly country, but among the best scenery on this map, and easy to reach from Brig.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Three separate cable cars from the valley floor - Morel to Riederalp, Betten to Bettmeralp, Fiesch to Fiescheralp - all run all year because the villages are car-free and have no road. Bike carriage is normal here; check aletscharena.ch for bike fare before travelling.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 19 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.aletscharena.ch/en/activities/biking">Aletsch Arena</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>8.067003,46.391337,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>aletsch</value></Data>
