  <Placemark>
    <name>Auron (Saint-Etienne-de-Tinee) [20 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Blainon 2105 m - top of the Blainon chairlift</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>The Tinee valley's gravity centre, and the easiest of the Nice parks to get a full day out of: marked descents drop nearly 500 m off Blainon straight back into the village, with a second, gentler sector above the Pinatelle gondola and the Lieuson chairlift. Grassy and fast up high, forested and rooty lower down.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Bike day pass 20 EUR, half day 15 EUR, single ride 10 EUR. Season pass 130 EUR for Auron alone, or 150 EUR for the Mercantour pass that also covers Isola 2000. Lifts run 4 July to 30 August 2026; the Las Donnas cable car is out for maintenance. A Cimes du Mercantour card (1.50 EUR) is needed on top of the pass.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 4 July; closed from 31 August (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Nice</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://ete.auron.com/en/activities/mountain-biking/">Auron</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>6.928080,44.207730,0</coordinates></Point>
