  <Placemark>
    <name>Col de la Madone / Ravin du Rank (above Menton) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Col de la Madone 925 m - road pass above Menton</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Not a park: one serious trail, and a famous road climb to reach it. The Ravin du Rank drops off the col towards Gorbio, 2.8 km for 550 m of descent, graded T5 with E2 exposure - loose, brittle limestone and long sequences of built stone steps that will find the limits of your suspension and your nerve. Ridden downhill only; walking back up means carrying the bike the whole way. Sea views the entire descent, and ridable in January.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Nothing to pay and nothing to ride up in. The col is the road climb the pros use for testing, about 900 m of ascent from Menton by Sainte-Agnes or by Peille. Shuttling by car is the usual alternative.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; T5 and exposed. Scout the step sections on foot before you commit - this is not a graded bike park run.</p><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure in a typical year; check local conditions.<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Menton</td><td>Bike</td><td>~1h15 climb</td></tr><tr><td>Nice</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://vttour.fr/sentiers/83">VTTour Ravin du Rank</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>7.423330,43.803110,0</coordinates></Point>
