  <Placemark>
    <name>Whistler Mountain Bike Park (British Columbia) [day pass, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Fitzsimmons Express top 1020 m - the bike park's main unload</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>The one every other bike park is measured against. Around eighty machine-built and natural trails over four zones: Fitzsimmons for the famous flow - A-Line, Dirt Merchant, Crank It Up - Garbanzo above it for longer and steeper, Creekside for the quiet side, and the Peak zone for Top of the World, a high alpine descent of roughly 1500 m. Green jump lines through to double-black tech, and the trail crew rebuilds constantly.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Fitzsimmons Express chair lifts riders out of Whistler Village; Garbanzo, Creekside and the Peak chair extend the terrain as the season opens up. The park runs mid-May to mid-October, with the Peak zone typically only from July to early September. Adult single-day tickets ran roughly 95-130 CAD in 2026 depending on date and how far ahead you book - we have not verified a fixed 2026 figure, so check whistlerblackcomb.com.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 May; closed from 16 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-20:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Vancouver</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.whistlerblackcomb.com/explore-the-resort/activities-and-events/whistler-mountain-bike-park.aspx">Whistler Blackcomb</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
