  <Placemark>
    <name>Mont-Sainte-Anne (Quebec) [gondola, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Summit 800 m - top of L'Etoile Filante gondola</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>North America's oldest World Cup downhill hill, and still one of its most punishing: the mountain's reputation is built on wet granite, roots and off-camber rock rather than machine-built berms. About 615 m of vertical under the gondola, roughly thirty downhill runs from beginner-graded flow to the World Cup track, and a cross-country and singletrack network that brings the mountain's total to around 175 km. It joined the Crankworx circuit as the 2026 World Tour finale.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>L'Etoile Filante gondola carries bikes to the summit; two chairlifts serve the lower mountain. Summer day tickets are sold through the resort's own ticket site and we could not confirm a 2026 mountain-bike rate, so check mont-sainte-anne.com before you go.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 16 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Quebec City</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://mont-sainte-anne.com/en/mountain-biking/">Mont-Sainte-Anne</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
