  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Innsbruck - Muttereralm (Tirol) [57 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Muttereralm 1600 m - top of the Muttereralmbahn</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Ten trails over about 20 km, ten minutes from the middle of Innsbruck, which makes this the easiest world-class riding to reach without a car on the whole map. Blue flow through to black downhill race track, an extended top section and connectors between the lines, plus a Rookie Park with an airbag. Across the valley, the Nordkette Singletrail drops off the Seegrube at 1900 m and has a reputation as one of the hardest marked descents in Europe - a different lift, a different ticket, and not a beginner's afternoon.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Muttereralmbahn gondola from Mutters, reachable by tram from Innsbruck. Day pass 57 EUR at the window, from 44 EUR booked online at least three days ahead. Daily 9:00 to 17:00, late May to late October.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 25 May; closed from 26 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Published operating hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Innsbruck</td><td>Tram + gondola</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.bikepark-innsbruck.com/en/">Bikepark Innsbruck</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
