  <Placemark>
    <name>Engelberg - Jochpass (Obwalden) [42 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Jochpass 2205 m - top of the Jochpass chairlift</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>The Jochpass Trail is the reason to come: 4.5 km of flowtrail from the pass down to Trubsee, gentle curves and small jumps, with no technical difficulty and a genuinely spectacular setting under the Titlis. Lower down, the Hells-Bells Trail adds 1.6 km with berms and a few harder sections. Not a big park, but a very good day, and easy to reach from Lucerne without a car.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Titlis Xpress gondola from Engelberg at 1000 m to Trubsee, then the Jochpass chairlift. MTB day pass 42 CHF for 16 and over, 21 CHF for 6 to 15, valid Engelberg - Trubsee - Jochpass - Engstlenalp.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 19 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lucerne</td><td>Train</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Zurich</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.engelberg.ch/en/summer/biking/">Engelberg</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
