  <Placemark>
    <name>St. Moritz - Corviglia (Engadin) [lift pass, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Corviglia 2485 m - top of the Signalbahn and the Marguns gondola</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>High, wide and open, with the Engadin lakes below you for the whole descent. Corviglia is the hub: flow trails drop towards St. Moritz and Celerina, and the surrounding valley has one of the densest marked mountain-bike networks in Switzerland once you are willing to pedal between lifts. Not a bike park in the berms-and-tables sense, more a lift-served alpine playground.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Signalbahn from St. Moritz Dorf and the gondola from Celerina to Marguns both carry bikes. Engadin publishes summer tariffs seasonally and we could not confirm a 2026 bike day rate; check the operator.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 19 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Zurich</td><td>Train</td><td>~3h15</td></tr><tr><td>Chur</td><td>Train</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.engadin.ch/en/bike/">Engadin St. Moritz</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
