  <Placemark>
    <name>Morzine - Le Pleney (Portes du Soleil, FR) [38 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Le Pleney 1490 m - top of the Pleney gondola</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>The other half of the Morzine-Les Gets pairing, and the classic base for a Portes du Soleil trip: lifts run in every direction from town, and by lunchtime you can be in Switzerland. The Pleney holds the historic downhill runs straight back into the village, and the Prodains lift up to Avoriaz opens the high, rockier riding around the Lindarets and the Swiss border.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Pleney gondola from the middle of Morzine at 985 m; the Prodains Express 3S serves Avoriaz. Portes du Soleil day pass 38 EUR online, season 438 EUR - the same ticket as Les Gets, Chatel and Champery.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 19 June; closed from 13 September (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Geneva</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h50</td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://en.morzine-avoriaz.com/discover-morzine/summer/mountain-biking/">Morzine</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
