  <Placemark>
    <name>La Clusaz (Aravis, FR) [23.50 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Beauregard 1630 m - top of the Beauregard gondola</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Six downhill runs and five enduro lines off the Beauregard and the Cret du Merle, inside a wider network of 125 km of marked trails across the Aravis. Steeper and more wooded than the big Tarentaise parks, and small enough to ride everything in a day. The village at the bottom is a genuine mountain town rather than a purpose-built base.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Beauregard gondola from the village at 1040 m, plus the Cret du Merle and Cret du Loup chairlifts. Bike day pass 23.50 EUR adult, 19 EUR child.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 13 June; closed from 20 September (published 2026 dates). Weekends in June and September, daily 1 July to 30 August.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Geneva</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Annecy</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.laclusaz.com/en/mountain-biking/">La Clusaz</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
