  <Placemark>
    <name>Samoens - Grand Massif (FR) [33 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Samoens 1600 - top of the Grand Massif Express</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>The Grand Massif Express climbs almost 900 m out of the valley floor, which gives Samoens some of the longest continuous descents in Haute-Savoie. The bike park itself is moderate rather than extreme, but the pass covers Flaine, Les Carroz and Morillon too, so an enduro day linking four resorts is the real draw.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Grand Massif Express gondola from Samoens at 700 m. A Grand Massif pedestrian and bike day pass is 33 EUR and covers the whole domain; single-resort day passes at Les Carroz and Morillon are 20-21 EUR.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 31 August (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Geneva</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.samoens.com/en/mountain-biking/">Samoens</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
