  <Placemark>
    <name>Serre Chevalier (Hautes-Alpes, FR) [28 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Ratier 1895 m - top of the Ratier gondola, Chantemerle</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>A big, sunny, south-facing domain strung along the Guisane valley, with four sectors and enough vertical that the descents to the valley floor go on far longer than you expect. Chantemerle and Villeneuve carry the bike park; the Serre Chevalier cable car above Ratier reaches 2470 m for the high traverses. Larch forest, dry dirt and 300 days of sun a year.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Ratier gondola from Chantemerle at 1360 m; the Casse du Boeuf chairlift at Villeneuve opens first each season. Bike day pass 28 EUR, two non-consecutive days 48.50 EUR, adult season 270.50 EUR.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 20 June; closed from 30 August (published 2026 dates). Chantemerle opens 27 June, Briancon and Monetier 4 July.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Grenoble</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr><tr><td>Marseille</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h00</td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.serre-chevalier.com/en/summer/bike">Serre Chevalier</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
