  <Placemark>
    <name>Sun Peaks Bike Park (British Columbia) [82 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sunburst 1850 m - top of the Sunburst Express</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Three mountains, high alpine terrain and a park that leans towards long, sustained descents rather than lap-the-jump-line repetition. Sunburst is the gravity hub; the cross-country network above the village is genuinely worth a day of its own. Quieter and cheaper than Whistler, with the same dry interior dirt as SilverStar two hours away.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Sunburst Express chairlift from the village at 1260 m. Adult day ticket 82 CAD at the window, up to 35% less booked online in advance.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 20 June; closed from 7 September (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Kamloops</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Vancouver</td><td>Car</td><td>~4h30</td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.sunpeaksresort.com/bike">Sun Peaks</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
