  <Placemark>
    <name>Fernie Alpine Resort (British Columbia) [lift ticket, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Elk Quad top 1365 m - the bike park's main unload</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Steep, raw and unmistakably Kootenay: loam, roots, rock rolls and old-growth cedar, on a mountain that gets enough rain to keep the dirt tacky when the Okanagan parks are blown out. The Elk Quad serves the park trails; the Timber Bowl and Great Bear chairs open the bigger terrain above. Not the place to learn, and much loved by people who already know how.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Elk Quad from the resort base at 1065 m, daily 10:00 to 16:00 and until 19:00 on Tuesdays and Thursdays. The resort sells day tickets through its own store; we could not confirm a 2026 adult rate, so check skifernie.com.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 25 June; closed from 7 September (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00<br/><small>Published hours; Tuesdays and Thursdays run until 19:00.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Calgary</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h00</td></tr><tr><td>Cranbrook</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://skifernie.com/summer/mountain-biking/">Fernie Alpine Resort</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
