  <Placemark>
    <name>Mont Sainte-Cecile (Quebec) [paid access, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mont Sainte-Cecile 895 m - pedal-access trail centre near Lac-Megantic</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>A young purpose-built network on a forested Appalachian mountain, with about 12 km of trails open by 2025 and further expansion underway. Five descents, one climbing trail and two traverses use roughly 285 m of vertical. The lower mountain has easier family and progression terrain plus a pump track; the south summit has intermediate and difficult trails; the north summit descents are very difficult and aimed at expert riders.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift: climb the signed ascent under your own power. Trail access is paid, but a current mountain-bike day price could not be confirmed. Bike and e-bike rental is available. Buy access and check conditions on the <a href="https://montstececile.square.site/">official Mont Sainte-Cecile site</a>.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 16 March; closed from 1 December (published 2026 tourism dates). Weather and mud closures can shorten the riding season.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lac-Megantic</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Sherbrooke</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Trail information and opening dates checked for 2026; verify current access before you go.</i>]]></description>
