  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Hakuba Iwatake Bike Park (Nagano) [4800 JPY]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Iwatake summit 1290 m - top of the Noah gondola</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>The gravity centre of the Hakuba Valley, with the Northern Alps filling the skyline across the valley. Alps Downhill is the signature run: 6.9 km of rolling berms that a confident beginner can ride and an expert can carry real speed down. Kamikaze Downhill is the opposite - steep, rooty, rock-gardened singletrack with a long-standing reputation. A pump track and skills area sit at the base.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Noah gondola lifts riders and bikes from 745 m to the 1290 m summit in about eight minutes. One-day gondola pass 4800 JPY for the bike park.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 25 April; closed from 15 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tokyo</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~3h30</td></tr><tr><td>Nagano</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://iwatake-mountain-resort.com/en/green/mountain-bike">Hakuba Iwatake</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
