  <Placemark>
    <name>Nevados de Chillan (Nuble, CL) [lift pass, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>El Refugio top 1840 m - the higher of the two bike lifts</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Seventeen trails on the flank of an active volcano, in araucaria and native forest: ten flow lines that suit a beginner, five fast enduro descents and two cross-country circuits. El Refugio is the newer lift and opens the harder terrain; El Tata covers the park pistes. It hosted the UCI Masters Mountain Bike World Championships in March 2026, on the Aguila downhill course and the Olimpico cross-country loop.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Two chairlifts take bikes, El Tata and El Refugio, both from Plaza Tata at 1535 m, where the ticket office, rental and cafe are. The park runs 10:00 to 16:45. Tickets load onto a rechargeable card; we could not confirm a 2026 bike day rate, so check nevadosdechillan.com.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 December; closed from 30 April (typical window; check the operator and conditions). Southern-hemisphere season.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:45<br/><small>Published operating hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Chillan</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Santiago</td><td>Car</td><td>~6h00</td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://nevadosdechillan.com/en/bike-park/">Nevados de Chillan</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
