  <Placemark>
    <name>La Parva (Santiago, CL) [lift pass, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>La Parva Base Camp 2765 m - bike park meeting point and lift base</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>One of the highest bike parks anywhere: about 10 km of trail across three runs, medium to expert, shaped by the French trail builder Jonathan Mahec, an hour and a half above Santiago. Big berms, drops and a lot of sky. Base Camp at the bottom has the cafe, parking and camping, and is the meeting point for the whole summer operation.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>One chairlift is adapted for bikes and lifts riders out of Base Camp. Reported day rates for the lift plus trails are around 10,000 CLP, but the operator's summer information is out of date and which lift runs varies by year - confirm with laparva.cl before driving up. The pin marks Base Camp rather than a top station for that reason.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 December; closed from 1 April (typical window; check the operator and conditions). Weekends only in parts of the season.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Santiago</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.laparva.cl/">La Parva</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
