  <Placemark>
    <name>Valle de Bravo - Monte Alto (MX) [shuttle, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Parque Estatal Monte Alto 2120 m - the main trail area</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Mexico's best-known mountain-bike town, an hour and a half west of Mexico City above a lake. Monte Alto is the marked and maintained core - pine and oak forest, well signed, views down onto the town - and there are seven distinct riding areas around the valley in total, from beginner loops to steep downhill used for national races.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Local operators run vans up from the town centre and pick you up at the bottom; you can also pedal, since the climb from the lake is only a few hundred metres. Trail access itself is free.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 November; closed from 1 June (typical window; check the operator and conditions). The summer rains are the off season.<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Mexico City</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr><tr><td>Toluca</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.trailforks.com/region/valle-de-bravo/">Trailforks Valle de Bravo</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
