  <Placemark>
    <name>Buen Camino Bike Park (San Mateo, CR) [25 USD, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>San Mateo, Alajuela - access town for the park (pin approximate)</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>A purpose-built 128-hectare bike park in tropical mountain forest an hour west of San Jose, and the most developed thing of its kind in Central America. Graded like a proper park: Viejo Verde as the green, El Patron and Jaguar as blues, Boss and Machete as double blacks, with jumps, wooden bridges and long sections of dense jungle. There is a restaurant and six cabins on site.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - you ride up and descend. Bike day pass 25 USD bought on site, hiking 15 USD; full-day bike rental about 130 USD. Open Wednesday to Monday, 08:00 to 16:00, closed Tuesdays. The park sits on Finca Ecologica El Bosque above San Mateo; it has no OpenStreetMap entry, so this pin marks the town rather than the gate.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure (normally open year-round).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-16:00<br/><small>Published Wednesday-Monday hours; closed Tuesday.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>San Jose</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Jaco</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.buencaminocostarica.com/">Buen Camino</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
