  <Placemark>
    <name>El Zur (Volcan de Agua, GT) [guided only, 90-199 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Trailhead about 2500 m on Volcan de Agua (pin approximate)</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Over 25 km of purpose-built singletrack cut into a private reserve on the flank of Volcan de Agua, above Antigua. Flowing and fast rather than brutal, dropping more than a vertical kilometre through coffee country and cloud forest, and almost certainly the best-built trail network in Central America. Almost nobody has ridden it, because you cannot get to it on your own.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift: a 4x4 shuttle takes you and the bike to about 2500 m. The reserve is private and closed except to landowners and to Old Town Outfitters in Antigua, who charge 90 to 199 USD per person depending on group size, lunch included, for a 4 to 5 hour trip starting at 08:00. The exact trailhead is not public, so this pin is the 2500 m contour on the north flank, not a surveyed point.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 November; closed from 1 May (typical window; check the operator and conditions). Dry season riding.<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Antigua Guatemala</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Guatemala City</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.oldtownoutfitters.com/">Old Town Outfitters</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
