  <Placemark>
    <name>Bike Park Pohorje Maribor (SI) [36.50-49 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Pohorska Vzpenjaca, Maribor - World Cup gravity park</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>A proper gondola-served park descending almost into Maribor, with progression from the green 2.4 km Family Line to flow and jump lines, red hand-built enduro trails and the legendary black World Cup course. World Cup drops 431 m over 2 km through roots, rocks, speed and large jumps; Fury adds steep natural corners and drops, while the expanded Areh zone provides more family, flow and technical riding.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Pohorska Vzpenjaca gondola serves the main hill, with additional lifts in the Areh zone. Adult 2026 day passes are 36.50-44 EUR on weekdays depending on period and 49 EUR Friday-Sunday and holidays. Gravity Card is accepted. The lower Family Line can sometimes operate outside the main season when snow-free, but check the live trail and lift status.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 11 March; closed from 1 December (published opening and 2026 season-pass end used as the practical season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Maribor centre</td><td>Bus / bike</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Graz</td><td>Car</td><td>~55 min</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.visitpohorje.si/en/bike-park-pohorje-maribor-awaits-its-first-visitors/">official 2026 opening notice</a>, <a href="https://www.visitpohorje.si/kolesarski-park-mariborsko-pohorje/">official trail descriptions</a> and <a href="https://www.visitpohorje.si/ceniki/kolesarski-park/">official 2026 prices</a>.</i>]]></description>
