  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Parnitha Enduro (Athens, GR) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mount Parnitha above Athens - rocky Mediterranean enduro</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>The most established gravity-oriented natural riding area near Athens, with pine and fir forest, exposed limestone, loose rock, fast earth and technical descents between roughly 1000 m and the lower foothills. A representative guided route is about 30 km with 600 m of climbing and roughly 50 percent trail. This is an informal shared-use network rather than a signed park, and route choice matters after fires or forestry work.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No bike lift. Pedal from the foothills, self-shuttle by road, or book a guided vehicle-assisted day; one published guided option starts from 85 EUR per person for a group of five, with bike rental extra. Carry offline mapping and yield to walkers.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Wildfire danger can close the mountain at short notice. Do not ride during official fire restrictions, and avoid wet limestone and peak summer heat.</p><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 October; closed from 1 June (typical cool-season window, not an official opening calendar). Check fire restrictions and local trail reports.<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Athens centre</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Athens airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/><i>Sources: <a href="https://www.aegeantrails.com/guided-bike-tour/mount-parnitha-day-tour-athens/">Aegean Trails Parnitha enduro tour</a> and <a href="https://www.discovergreece.com/travel-ideas/best-of/7-most-popular-places-mountain-bike-greece">Discover Greece MTB destinations</a>. Seasonal dates are a conservative average.</i>]]></description>
