  <Placemark>
    <name>Dajti Mountain Enduro (Tirana, AL) [gondola]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Fusha e Dajtit above Tirana - natural forest riding with gondola access</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Albania's most accessible mountain riding zone, with informal routes from the Dajti plateau through beech and pine forest toward Tirana. Expect rough natural paths, rock, roots, steep sections and exceptional views over the capital and Adriatic plain rather than shaped or graded bike-park runs. Formal waymarking and maintenance remain limited, so a guide or strong offline navigation is recommended.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Dajti Ekspres reaches the plateau and is reported to carry bikes, giving access without a full road climb. Confirm bicycle acceptance before travelling because operating rules can change. Road shuttles and pedalling are alternatives; there is no dedicated bike patrol or uplift ticket.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Shared national-park terrain: control speed around walkers, respect closures and do not assume every hiking path permits or suits bikes.</p><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 March; closed from 1 December (typical riding window). Low trails may be rideable in winter; check gondola operation, rain and snow conditions.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-18:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tirana centre</td><td>Car / bus</td><td>~25 min to gondola</td></tr><tr><td>Tirana airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/><i>Sources: <a href="https://akt.gov.al/en/attractions/Dajti-Mountain-National-Park/">Albanian tourism authority</a> and <a href="https://www.albania-spirit.com/guides/cycling-albania/">2026 Albania cycling guide</a>. Seasonal dates are an average.</i>]]></description>
