  <Placemark>
    <name>Saint-Lary Bike Park (Pyrenees) [26 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bouleaux chairlift summit 2215 m - maintained riding above Pla d'Adet</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>More than 40 km of marked green-to-black trails between 2215 m and 1700 m. Family Rider and Easy Rider provide genuine progression terrain, while Woodstock brings long flow and wood features; K-Bourre and Razorback supply the technical black riding. Ten maintained trails and an initiation zone make this one of the most complete parks in the French Pyrenees.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The detachable Bouleaux chairlift carries bikes. The 2026 adult day pass is 22.50 EUR from Pla d'Adet or 26 EUR including the cable car from Saint-Lary village.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 31 August (published 2026 dates). The opening weekend uses the Bouleaux chairlift only; daily operation runs from 4 July through 30 August.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tarbes</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h10</td></tr><tr><td>Toulouse</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://saint-lary.altiservice.com/en/activities/bike-park/">official Saint-Lary bike park page</a>; check weather and lift status.</i>]]></description>
