  <Placemark>
    <name>Sierra Nevada Bike Park (Granada, ES) [lift price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Veleta sector 3030 m to Pradollano 2150 m - high-alpine Spanish riding</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Six downhill circuits descend from the exposed terrain near Veleta toward Borreguiles and Pradollano, complemented by a cross-country circuit at Fuente Alta. The huge elevation, loose rock and open high-mountain character make this very different from a forest bike park; weather and trail availability can change quickly.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer access uses the Borreguiles gondola and Veleta chairlift. A current bike-specific 2026 day rate was not clearly published, so confirm both bicycle carriage and open bike trails before travelling.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 11 July; closed from 24 August (published 2026 summer-lift dates). Individual bike trails may have a shorter window or remain closed depending on maintenance and conditions.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Granada</td><td>Car / bus</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Malaga</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/><i>Sources: <a href="https://sierranevada.es/en/summer/the-resort/calendar-and-rates/">official 2026 summer calendar</a> and Sierra Nevada bike park information; verify current trail status.</i>]]></description>
