  <Placemark>
    <name>The GAP Bikepark (Dublin, IE) [shuttle price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Glencullen Adventure Park - purpose-built gravity riding above Dublin</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>A compact proper bike park with blue, red and black descents, jump lines and high-consequence expert features. The blue and red trails provide progression, but difficulty rises quickly and the hardest lines are aimed at confident gravity riders.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Five vans and bike trailers provide scheduled uplift, with pedal access also possible. Prices depend on the booked session and were not reliably verified here; reserve through the official site.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br>Normally open year-round on scheduled operating days; severe weather and forestry work can cause closures.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Dublin centre</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Dublin airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://thegap.ie/trails/">official GAP trail page</a>; advance booking recommended.</i>]]></description>
