  <Placemark>
    <name>BikePark Wales (Wales, UK) [uplift price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Gethin Woods above Merthyr Tydfil - the UK's largest gravity trail network</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>More than fifty all-weather trails cover genuine beginner progression, high-speed flow, jumps and steep technical race-style terrain. Kermit provides a long green introduction, while the red, black and pro lines make the park a destination for experienced riders as well.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Dedicated vehicles provide booked uplift, or riders can buy pedal and e-bike access. Dynamic session prices were not reliably exposed, so check the official booking calendar.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Normally open year-round on scheduled days. Booking availability, storms and trail work can affect individual dates.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Cardiff</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bristol</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.bikeparkwales.com/">official BikePark Wales site</a>; uplift booking is strongly recommended.</i>]]></description>
