  <Placemark>
    <name>Dyfi Bike Park (Wales, UK) [uplift price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Dyfi Forest - big-mountain gravity trails built by the Athertons</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>A 650-acre destination with hand-built red through triple-black trails. Long, fast and technical descents combine natural rock and roots with large jumps and race-scale features. There is no beginner terrain: even the red trails require solid bike-park skills.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Land Rover shuttles provide uplift from the base. Prices and operating days vary through the booking calendar, so reserve directly with the park.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Normally open year-round on selected booked days, subject to Welsh mountain weather and maintenance closures.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Aberystwyth</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Manchester</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.dyfibikepark.co.uk/">official Dyfi Bike Park site</a>; advance booking required.</i>]]></description>
