  <Placemark>
    <name>Nevis Range (Fort William, UK) [39.85 GBP online]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Aonach Mor 650 m gondola station - World Cup downhill above Fort William</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Three major gondola descents: the legendary orange World Cup track, tight technical black Top Chief and the more approachable Blue Doon. Lower Witches trails add year-round pedal-access riding below the gondola. Highland weather, rocks and sustained vertical make even the easier mountain line demanding.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Mountain Gondola carries riders and bikes in about fifteen minutes. The 2026 adult online multi-trip uplift is 39.85 GBP, or 41.95 GBP at the ticket office.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 May; closed from 1 October (typical bike-uplift window). Lower trails remain open year-round, while gondola dates and individual descents depend on weather, events and maintenance.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Fort William</td><td>Car / bus</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Glasgow</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h45</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.nevisrange.co.uk/activities/bike/uplift-prices/">official Nevis Range 2026 uplift page</a>; check the daily mountain report.</i>]]></description>
