  <Placemark>
    <name>Glentress 7stanes (Scotland, UK) [no lift, parking fee]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Glentress Forest - 75 km of purpose-built Tweed Valley singletrack</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Scotland's flagship trail centre ranges from green family loops and blue progression trails to long red and black routes. Modern flow finales sit alongside classic rooty and rocky forest singletrack, with enough climbing and distance for full-day rides.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift: all official routes are pedal-accessed. Trails are free, with all-day parking charged at the visitor centre; bike hire, coaching, showers and food are available.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Normally open year-round. Forestry work, storms and repairs regularly divert or close individual sections, so check current notices.<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Edinburgh</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Edinburgh</td><td>Bus</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://forestryandland.gov.scot/visit/destinations/glentress/bike">Forestry and Land Scotland</a>; follow live diversions.</i>]]></description>
