  <Placemark>
    <name>Enduro Trails Bielsko-Biala (PL) [no lift, free trails]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Blonia trail centre - Poland's best-known pedal-access enduro network</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>A large signed network on the wooded hills above Bielsko-Biala, combining machine-built flow with technical natural enduro. Climbing trails link green and blue progression lines to red and black descents; the area hosted Enduro World Cup racing.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift at the main Blonia network: climb the signed uphill trails. Trail access is free, with rentals, coaching and services available at the base.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (typical window). Respect wet-weather, forestry and event closures.<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-18:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Katowice</td><td>Car / train</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Krakow</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://endurotrails.pl/en">official Enduro Trails site</a>; check current trail status.</i>]]></description>
