  <Placemark>
    <name>Szczyrk Bike Park by Trek (PL) [lift price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Szczyrk Mountain Resort - lift-served Beskid flow and downhill</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>One-way purpose-built trails spread across the resort, from smoother blue flow and a progressive skill zone to red, black and competition-level downhill. The park hosts major Polish and European DH racing.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Gondola and chairlifts provide bike uplift. Current 2026 bike-pass prices are sold through the resort and were not reliably exposed here.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 May; closed from 1 November (typical lift window; shoulder-season operation may be weekends only).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Katowice</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Krakow</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.szczyrkowski.pl/en/resort/szczyrk-news/szczyrk-mountain-resort-news">official Szczyrk 2026 news</a>; verify open lifts and trails.</i>]]></description>
