  <Placemark>
    <name>Pilat Enduro Trails (near Lyon, FR) [no lift, free trails]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Croix de Chaubouret above Saint-Etienne - official natural enduro network</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Six official enduro itineraries cross the varied Pilat massif, from shorter intermediate descents to the 18.6 km Col du Gratteau route with roughly 1100 m of climbing. These are shared natural paths rather than closed bike-park tracks, combining forest singletrack, rock, roots and linking climbs.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no mandatory trail fee. Ride the routes as pedal-powered itineraries or arrange your own point-to-point transport; riders must yield to walkers.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 March; closed from 1 December (typical riding window). Snow, freeze-thaw, storms and forestry work can shorten the season.<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Saint-Etienne</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Lyon</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h10</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.pilat-tourisme.fr/planifier/activites-et-detente/velo-et-vtt/nos-circuits-vtt/enduro">official Pilat enduro route page</a>; shared paths are not downhill-only tracks.</i>]]></description>
