  <Placemark>
    <name>Gochang MTB Park (Jeonbuk, KR) [no public uplift verified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bangjangsan foothills at Gochang - one of South Korea's established downhill parks</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>A purpose-built mountain-bike park used for Korean downhill and cross-country riding, with steep forest race lines, rock, roots and technical features. The terrain is best suited to experienced riders; inspect features and current course conditions before committing.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No dependable public lift or shuttle service was verified. Plan to pedal or push unless a race or local organizer announces vehicle uplift. No current mandatory access price was published.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 March; closed from 1 December (typical regional riding window). The official listed hours are 09:00-17:00 and the facility is closed on Mondays; weather or events can change access.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Published hours; closed Monday.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Gwangju</td><td>Car</td><td>~55 min</td></tr><tr><td>Jeonju</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.gochang.go.kr/tour/board/view.gochang?boardId=BBS_TOUR&amp;categoryCode1=TOUR03&amp;dataSid=157491&amp;menuCd=DOM_000000402002003000&amp;orderBy=TAG_ID%20ASC%2CDATA_SID%20DESC&amp;paging=ok&amp;startPage=1">official Gochang tourism listing</a>; verify course status locally.</i>]]></description>
