  <Placemark>
    <name>Nanji Hangang Extreme Bike Park (Seoul, KR) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Nanji Hangang Park - compact beginner MTB skills course in Seoul</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>South Korea's first flat-site MTB practice course recreates small mountain contours and slopes in a 5,425 square metre facility. Its 450 m circuit is designed for beginner and intermediate riders to practise bike handling safely. It is a useful city session spot, not a destination downhill park.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift is needed on the compact circuit. No current admission charge was published; helmets and suitable protective equipment are required.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round. Published hours are 09:00-18:00 in summer and 09:00-16:00 in winter; severe weather or maintenance can close the course.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-18:00<br/><small>Published summer hours; winter closes at 16:00.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Central Seoul</td><td>Bike / metro and bike</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://data.visitkorea.or.kr/resource/1029885">Korea Tourism Organization facility listing</a>.</i>]]></description>
