    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Santa Elena / Medellin Enduro (CO) [shuttle, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Santa Elena plateau above Medellin - informal gravity network</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Pine and cloud-forest singletrack descends from the cool plateau toward the Aburra valley, ranging from flowing local lines to steep, rooty and technical enduro. Routes are unsigned, change frequently and share land with walkers and farmers.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Use a local 4x4 shuttle, guide, or pedal the roads from Santa Elena. The Arvi Metrocable is useful for visiting the plateau, but bicycle carriage and direct access to gravity trails must be confirmed before relying on it.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; January-February and July-August are normally driest. Do not ride saturated cloud-forest trails.<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Medellin centre</td><td>Car / local bus</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/><i>Sources: <a href="https://www.medellin.travel/santa-elena/?lang=en">official Medellin tourism guide</a> and <a href="https://www.medellin.gov.co/es/corregimientos/gerencia/santa-elena/">Medellin municipality</a>. Ride with local knowledge.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-75.5020,6.2100,0</coordinates></Point>
