  <Placemark>
    <name>Bukit Kiara Trails (Kuala Lumpur, MY) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bukit Kiara - volunteer-maintained urban jungle network</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>A dense network of roughly 90 named trails, from approachable loops to root-heavy technical all-mountain and downhill lines such as the harder local classics. Trails were built and maintained by riders but are intentionally shared with hikers and runners.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Free pedal access; no lift. Climb the tarmac spine or trail connectors, yield to every non-rider and never build or modify lines without local approval.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round, but do not ride during or immediately after tropical downpours.<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Central Kuala Lumpur</td><td>Car / metro and bike</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/><i>Sources: <a href="https://www.fobk.org/trails/">Friends of Bukit Kiara</a> and <a href="https://www.traks.org.my/">TRAKS Malaysia</a>.</i>]]></description>
