  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Dali / Shaxi Tea-Horse Trails (Yunnan, CN) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Dali and the ancient Tea-Horse corridor - highland adventure MTB</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Old stone roads, pine-forest paths, village tracks and high passes connect Bai and Tibetan cultural landscapes between Dali, Shaxi and the northwest Yunnan highlands. This is guided expedition riding, not a signed bike park.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No bike lift. Commercial guides use vehicle transfers for point-to-point routes; confirm permissions because many famous hiking or heritage paths are not automatically bike routes.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Best March-May and September-November; summer monsoon mud and winter snow affect high routes.<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Dali</td><td>Guide vehicle</td><td>Local / multi-day</td></tr></table><br/><i>Regional adventure-riding pin centred on Dali; use a local MTB guide and verify each route.</i><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.bikechina.com/">Bike China</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
