    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Western Sichuan / Four Sisters MTB (CN) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Qionglai and Tibetan Plateau foothills - high-altitude expedition riding</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Remote roads and mountain tracks rise from the Sichuan basin toward Tibetan plateau scenery around the Four Sisters range. Expect major altitude, long climbs, rough surfaces and expedition logistics rather than gravity laps.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Book a local guide and support vehicle; route permissions and foreign-traveller restrictions can change.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Best May-June and September-October. Monsoon landslides, snow and altitude are serious constraints.<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Chengdu</td><td>Guide vehicle</td><td>~4h to Rilong</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.bikechina.com/guided-bike-tours/western-sichuan-four-sister-mountain-6-day-tour">Bike China Four Sisters itinerary</a>.</i>]]></description>
