      <mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Kahakapao / Makawao Forest Reserve (Maui, US) [no lift, free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Maui's main purpose-built forest trail centre</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>The Pineapple Express one-way descent drops about 400 m over 3.4 km with tabletops, a wooden berm and beginner ride-arounds. Renegade adds mixed cross-country and downhill terrain, while three skills areas progress from novice berms and a teeter to pump tracks and expert wooden step-up jumps.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Free pedal access; no uplift. Climb the forest roads and signed trail network from the Kahakapao trailhead.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round, but avoid riding when wet or muddy. <br/>Daily opening hours: 07:00-18:00<br/><small>Daylight riding estimate; closures can follow heavy rain, storms or forestry work.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Kahului</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Makawao</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/><i>Sources: <a href="https://dlnr.hawaii.gov/recreation/nah/maui/">Hawaii DLNR Na Ala Hele</a> and the <a href="https://dlnr.hawaii.gov/forestry/files/2026/03/DRAFT-Makawao-FR-Management-Plan-Public-Review.pdf">2026 Makawao Forest Reserve management plan</a>.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-156.2478,20.8207,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>kahakapao-makawao</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bikepark</value></Data>
      <Data name="open_from"><value>01-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>01-01</value></Data>
      <mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>West Maui Bike Park (Napili, US) [no lift, free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Community dirt-jump and skills park in Napili</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>A five-acre community bike park with progressive dirt-jump lines, pump and skills terrain developed by the Maui Mountain Bike Coalition with input from Cam Zink. It is a compact practice park rather than a mountain descent.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Free pedal access; no lift. Pedal or push back to the start of each line. Pedal bikes only.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; it closes for rain, saturated ground or high winds. <br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-18:00<br/><small>Published daily hours; weather closures apply.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lahaina</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Kahului</td><td>Car</td><td>~55 min</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.mauimountainbike.org/westmauibikepark">Maui Mountain Bike Coalition</a>. Check its channels for weather closures.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-156.6690,20.9978,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
