      <mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Peacock Flats / Kuaokala (Oahu, US) [permit access, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Remote Waianae ridge riding above Oahu's northwest coast</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Rough ridge roads and steep, technical rainforest singletrack connect the Peacock Flats camping area and Kuaokala zone, with exposed ocean views and loose, eroded sections. This is remote natural riding, not a maintained bike park.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Access through the Space Force tracking-station road is controlled; obtain the required state permit and carry identification. Expect a substantial pedal and route-finding.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round when access is open; avoid storms, mud and high fire-risk closures.<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Honolulu</td><td>Car + pedal</td><td>~1h30 to gate</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://dlnr.hawaii.gov/dofaw/fw-announcements/access-restored-to-public-lands-on-west-o%CA%BBahu-via-the-space-force-satellite-tracking-station-road/">Hawaii DLNR access notice</a>. Verify permits and gate arrangements before departure.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-158.1890,21.5740,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
