      <mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>St Louis Heights / Waahila Ridge (Oahu, US) [access must be checked, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Steep Honolulu ridge terrain with uncertain bike access</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>The forested ridge above St Louis Heights has steep roots, clay, narrow natural lines and short technical descents. It is shared hiking terrain rather than a sanctioned bike park, and bicycle permission can vary by segment.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal from town, but confirm locally that every intended trail permits bicycles; yield to walkers and do not ride closed or hiking-only paths.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Potentially rideable year-round, but wet red clay becomes slick and damaging. Access status is not sufficiently documented for a destination trip.<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Waikiki</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/><i>Indicative local riding-zone pin only. Confirm legal bicycle access with Hawaii trail managers before riding.</i><br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://dlnr.hawaii.gov/recreation/nah/oahu/">Hawaii DLNR trails</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-157.7985,21.3118,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>st-louis-heights-oahu</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>expert natural</value></Data>
      <Data name="open_from"><value>01-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>01-01</value></Data>
      <mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Papenoo Valley (Tahiti, PF) [backcountry, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Tahiti's volcanic interior adventure route</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>A rough valley road and connecting tracks enter a deep volcanic canyon through rainforest, river crossings and waterfall country. It is scenic backcountry and expedition-style riding, not a signed singletrack park.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Ride out-and-back or arrange a local guide and 4x4 support. River depth, landslides and private or controlled sections can alter the route.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Best in the drier May-October period; avoid heavy rain because rivers rise quickly and surfaces become hazardous.<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Papeete</td><td>Car + bike</td><td>~45 min to valley mouth</td></tr></table><br/><i>Sources: <a href="https://www.tahititourisme.jp/natural-heritage/papenoo-valley-maroto/">Tahiti Tourisme Papenoo Valley</a> and local bike rental or guide advice.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-149.4260,-17.6210,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>papenoo-valley</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>expert natural</value></Data>
      <Data name="open_from"><value>05-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>11-01</value></Data>
      <mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Moorea Pineapple Route / Opunohu (PF) [shared tracks, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Plantation tracks beneath Moorea's volcanic peaks</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Farm roads and mixed natural tracks wind through pineapple plantations in the Opunohu interior, with connections toward Belvedere viewpoints. Expect scenic cross-country and adventure riding rather than a formal bike park or continuous gravity singletrack.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Rent a mountain bike locally and pedal from the coast. Stay on permitted routes, respect plantation work and ask before entering private tracks.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; May-October is generally drier. Tropical rain can turn clay tracks muddy very quickly.<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tahiti</td><td>Ferry + bike</td><td>~45 min ferry</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://tahititourisme.pf/en-pf/islands-and-archipelagos/the-society-islands/moorea/escape-to-moorea/">Tahiti Tourisme - Moorea</a>.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-149.8370,-17.5260,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>moorea-opunohu</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner natural</value></Data>
      <Data name="open_from"><value>01-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>01-01</value></Data>
      <mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Domaine de Deva MTB (Bourail, NC) [no lift, free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>New Caledonia's major coastal trail park</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>An extensive marked network crosses dry forest, ridges and lagoon-facing terrain, with green family riding through technical red routes. Individual circuits include the 12.4 km Blue Riviere de Deva loop. Trails are unsupervised.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Free pedal access; no lift. Start from the Domaine de Deva reception and choose a signed loop appropriate to conditions.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round, but wildfire danger, storms or maintenance can close the domain. <br/>Daily opening hours: 06:30-19:00<br/><small>Published domain hours; fire-risk and weather closures apply.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Noumea</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h</td></tr><tr><td>Bourail</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.newcaledonia.travel/offers/mountain-bike-trail-n-9-blue-riviere-de-deva-bourail-en-3913712/">New Caledonia Tourism</a>. Check the domain's fire-risk status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>165.4750,-21.6050,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
