    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Queenstown Bike Park / Skyline Uplift (NZ) [gondola]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Ben Lomond's world-class gondola-served gravity network</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>More than 30 km of purpose-built downhill lines descend directly toward Queenstown, spanning approachable flow through jumps, roots and steep expert technical tracks. The public Ben Lomond trails are separate from the Skyline uplift operation.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Skyline's dedicated MTB gondola cabins carry riders and bikes from Brecon Street. A bike-uplift pass is required; 2026/27 standard pricing is due to be published on 1 August 2026.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Bike uplift is scheduled from 19 September 2026 to about 16 May 2027, weather dependent. The trail reserve can have separate fire, rain or maintenance closures. <br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-21:00<br/><small>Indicative gondola hours; the MTB uplift schedule varies by date and can stop for rain, lightning or reserve closures.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Queenstown centre</td><td>Bike</td><td>~5 min</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://queenstown.skyline.co.nz/things-to-do/mountain-bike-uplift/">official Skyline MTB uplift</a>. Check live uplift hours before riding.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>168.6472,-45.0251,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
