      <mwm:icon>Transport</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Trysil Bike Park (Norway) [chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Large progression-focused trail destination at Trysilfjellet</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Lift-served flow trails with berms, jumps and drops connect to the wider Trysil Bike Arena, including around 30 km of built trails near the main centre. Options range from family progression to fast expert lines.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Fjellekspressen chairlift carries bikes; a bike pass is required. Pedal-access trail networks remain available beyond lift days.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Published 2026 lift season: selected dates from 5 June through 11 October, daily 20 June-16 August and during autumn holidays. <br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00<br/><small>Published standard lift hours; selected evening extensions apply.</small><br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Oslo</td><td>Car / bus</td><td>~2h45</td></tr></table><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://www.trysil.com/stisykling/sommerapen-heis/">official 2026 summer lift schedule</a>.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>12.1645,61.3065,0</coordinates></Point>
