  <Placemark>
    <name>Jonkershoek / Stellenbosch MTB (South Africa) [permit, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>World-class Cape mountain and winelands trail network</b><br/><br/><b>Trails</b><br/>Long fire-road climbs feed rocky natural descents, flow trails, jumps and technical enduro lines around MTO Jonkershoek and the broader Stellenbosch network. The regional permit connects many neighbouring trail systems.<br/><br/><b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Buy the correct day or regional permit before entering; the MTB network is on MTO land near, but administratively distinct from, the CapeNature reserve.<br/><br/><b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round, best in the cooler dry periods. Fire danger, forestry work and winter storms cause closures.<br/><br/><b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Stellenbosch</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Cape Town</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/><i>Sources: <a href="https://winelandstrails.com/">Wine Lands Trails permit</a> and <a href="https://stellenboschtrailfund.co.za/">Stellenbosch Trail Fund</a>.</i>]]></description>
